e_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6XKtDc","user":{"login":"adriano-sudario","id":13634034,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzNjM0MDM0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13634034?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/adriano-sudario","html_url":"https://github.com/adriano-sudario","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adriano-sudario/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adriano-sudario/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adriano-sudario/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adriano-sudario/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adriano-sudario/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adriano-sudario/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adriano-sudario/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adriano-sudario/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/adriano-sudario/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-11T14:32:08Z","updated_at":"2024-12-11T14:32:08Z","body":"> This is not a bug, see:\r\n> \r\n>     * [Document `AudioStreamPlayer.get_playback_position()` intentionally aways returning `0.0` when using `AudioStreamInteractive` #99200](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99200)\r\n\r\nI still believe it makes a lot more sense to return the current clip's playback position than just returning 0.\r\nMaybe it could return -1 if more transitioning is happening? And then add this behavior to the documenation.\r\nWhat do you think?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2536165596/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2536172979","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100262#issuecomment-2536172979","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100262","id":2536172979,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6XKu2z","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-11T14:35:05Z","updated_at":"2024-12-11T14:35:05Z","body":"That'd be up to the audio team to decide, I just repeated what has been done recently","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2536172979/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2537504946","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100262#issuecomment-2537504946","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100262","id":2537504946,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6XP0Cy","user":{"login":"timoschwarzer","id":8849554,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg4NDk1NTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8849554?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer","html_url":"https://github.com/timoschwarzer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timoschwarzer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-12T00:49:47Z","updated_at":"2024-12-12T00:49:47Z","body":"I feel like returning 0 makes more sense here because this audio playback can have multiple streams play at the same time with different playback positions. I think there should be dedicated methods specifically for `AudioStreamPlaybackInteractive` to get playback positions of a specific stream by index/name and to get the stream indexes/names that are currently active and which state they are in (Fade In/Playing/Fade Out).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2537504946/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2579232144","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100262#issuecomment-2579232144","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100262","id":2579232144,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Zu_WQ","user":{"login":"basilicon","id":87910222,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3OTEwMjIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/87910222?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilicon","html_url":"https://github.com/basilicon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilicon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilicon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilicon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilicon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilicon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilicon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilicon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilicon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/basilicon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-09T05:51:09Z","updated_at":"2025-01-09T05:51:09Z","body":"If AudioStreamPlaybackInteractive is going to have dedicated methods for getting playback position for each stream anyways, could get_playback_position default to returning the playback position for the current stream, rather than doing nothing and returning 0?  I feel always returning 0 feels weird, since clearly if something is playing, the playback position should be nonzero.  The documentation could also specify that the returned playback position is only for the current stream, and recommends using those other methods for the other streams.\r\n\r\nAlso, I can't think of many use cases for get_playback_position (or even the other dedicated methods).  First and foremost, you can't use playback position with AudioStreamInteractive for AudioStreamPlayer's seek() or play() methods, as currently AudioStreamInteractive only plays streams from their beginnings.  The primary use for the get_playback_position method in this context is debugging, and I don't think it makes sense to have a debugging method always return 0.\r\n\r\nThis isn't totally related, but it might be nice to have some functionality for pausing/resuming AudioStreamInteractive's playback.  It would be useful for when you need to temporarily pause the game to open a menu or play a cutscene or something, but don't want to restart the current stream from the beginning when you unpause.  To me, this seems like the main reason why you might want to use a function like this in the first place; so you can stop playback and then resume it roughly where you left off.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2579232144/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]